35 | general | A stream called Rose Run: the 1st Texas was hurled back across it by the 124th New York | bld-rose-farm | 1863-07-02 (the name Rose Run as the study uses it; hedged by 'apparently') | hedged | The study says Benning apparently came up just as the Texas regiment was being hurled back across Rose Run by the bayonet charge of the 124th New York | =Benning, in the meantime, had {{percefved|perceived}} that Robertson was having difficulties in taking Houck's Ridge in his front and advanced [Ibid., p. 415], apparently coming up just as the Texas regiment was being hurled back across Rose Run by the bayonet charge of the 124th New York. ~O
