37 | fields | The 20th Georgia had to advance up the cleared triangular field | - | 1863-07-02 | stated | The study says the entire force of the 20th Georgia would have to advance up the cleared triangular field | =On their right was Colonel John Jones' 20th Georgia Regiment, whose entire force would have to advance up the cleared triangular field, whereas the 15th Georgia and {{ist|1st}} Texas were sheltered by the "wooded, rocky hill" of Rose Woods to the immediate left. ~O
37 | woodlots | Rose Woods was a wooded, rocky hill on the left of the cleared triangular field | bld-rose-farm | 1863-07-02 | stated | The study says the 15th Georgia and 1st Texas were sheltered by the wooded, rocky hill of Rose Woods to the immediate left of the cleared triangular field | =On their right was Colonel John Jones' 20th Georgia Regiment, whose entire force would have to advance up the cleared triangular field, whereas the 15th Georgia and {{ist|1st}} Texas were sheltered by the "wooded, rocky hill" of Rose Woods to the immediate left. ~O
